<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01J1">Warning <span data-tag="01J1">4.5.6.12</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a pullback diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ X'_{} \ar [d]^{q'} \ar [r]^-{f'} &amp;  X_{} \ar [d]^{q} \\ S'_{} \ar [r]^-{f} &amp;  S_{}, } \]
</div>
<p> where $q$ is an isofibration. If $f$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories, then $f'$ is also an equivalence of $\infty $-categories (Corollary <a data-tag="01HJ" href="/tag/01HJ">4.5.3.33</a>). Beware that if $f$ is merely assumed to be a categorical equivalence of simplicial sets, then it is not necessarily true that $f'$ is a categorical equivalence of simplicial sets. </p>
